<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  [XND] Nocturnal Animals (Continued) (Mlie.XNDNocturnalAnimals, Workshop 2269731409).

  That mod gives an animal a body clock through a mod extension on its race's ThingDef: Diurnal (the vanilla
  behaviour, and what an animal without the extension gets), Nocturnal, Crepuscular or Cathemeral. It deduces
  nothing from a vanilla field: it hand-lists defNames in its own 1.6/Patches/Core/*.xml (read 2026-10-13), so an
  animal it does not name stays diurnal.

  MG_TuSun (Pallas's cat, predator, body size 0.75) follows Lynx, the mod's wild small cat (body size 0.6):
  Nocturnal. Cat is not listed; it is a domestic cat, not a wild hunter.

  MG_TiaoShu (jerboa, small herbivorous rodent, body size 0.3) follows Chinchilla (herbivore, body size 0.35):
  Crepuscular. Rat is Nocturnal but is a pest omnivore.

  MG_Horse gets nothing: the mod does not list Horse, so a horse is diurnal, and this one is a horse breed.
  MG_TuBoShu (marmot) gets nothing: it is a ground squirrel, and the mod does not list Squirrel.

  Only applied when that mod is active; without it this file changes nothing and logs nothing.
  PatchOperationFindMod matches the mod's display name. No load order is asked: the extension is an XML node
  parsed after every assembly is loaded.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>[XND] Nocturnal Animals (Continued)</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
					<xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="MG_TuSun"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<li Class="NocturnalAnimals.ExtendedRaceProperties">
							<bodyClock>Nocturnal</bodyClock>
						</li>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
					<xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="MG_TiaoShu"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<li Class="NocturnalAnimals.ExtendedRaceProperties">
							<bodyClock>Crepuscular</bodyClock>
						</li>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
